2118358019||mws_KeepCameraStill_help|Witcher Senses no longer move the camera: no zoom and no shift.
2118358020||mws_RemoveEdgeDimming_help|No darkened, desaturated edges around the screen while Witcher Senses are on. This only matters with Highlight Style: Glow. With Highlight Style: Markers or None the edges are never dimmed.
2118358021||mws_RemoveSounds_help|No sound when Witcher Senses start and stop.
2118358022||mws_KeepAmbientSound_help|The world keeps its normal sound while Witcher Senses are on.
2118358023||mws_InstantHighlights_help|The game's highlights appear and disappear at once, instead of after a delay.
2118358024||mws_HighlightStyle_help|Markers: small markers over herbs, containers, doors, clues, trails, corpses and hostile creatures, hidden behind walls and fading with distance.<br>Glow: the game's glowing highlights.<br>None: no highlights at all, which makes clues hard to find.
2118358025||mws_RemoveRemainsHighlight_help|No sparkle over lootable corpses while Witcher Senses are on.
2118358026||mws_AllowJumpSprint_help|Jumping and sprinting stay possible while Witcher Senses are on.
2118358027||mws_RemoveSoundCircles_help|No gray and red circles around the creatures Witcher Senses let you hear.
2118358028||option_mws_RedContainers|Red Owned Containers
2118358029||preset_value_mws_RedContainers_0|Only When a Guard Is in Reach
2118358030||preset_value_mws_RedContainers_1|Always
2118358031||mws_RedContainers_help|A container that belongs to someone gets a red marker, because taking from it is stealing.<br>Only When a Guard Is in Reach: only while a guard is close enough to notice.<br>Always: every owned container.
2118358039||option_mws_FocusToggle|Toggle Witcher Senses (Instead of Hold)
2118358040||mws_FocusToggle_help|Press once to turn Witcher Senses on and again to turn them off. This is the same setting as in the game's Accessibility options.
